      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Let $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where ${b}_{1}=4{c}_{2}$ and ${b}_{2}=-2{c}_{1}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-3{c}_{1}-5{c}_{2} \\\\  & =-5{c}_{2}-3{c}_{1} \\\\  & =-5({c}_{2})+3(-{c}_{1}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}(4{c}_{2})+\\frac{3}{2}(-2{c}_{1}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}{b}_{1}+\\frac{3}{2}{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}].$",
